# --- DD Design Companion ---
# Rule of thumb: if the SPA doesn't load it at runtime (or the build/sync tools
# don't need it), it doesn't belong in this public repo.

# This SPA ships ZERO npm dependencies — the build (build-data.mjs), sync
# (sync-icons.mjs) and preview (serve.mjs) are all vanilla Node. node_modules /
# package*.json only ever appear from ad-hoc dev tooling (e.g. jsdom for a test
# pass) and must never be committed. If the build ever takes a real dependency,
# revisit this and commit a curated package.json.
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json

# logs / OS / editor cruft
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# scratch / test files
_test*.mjs
*.tmp

# raw / intermediate data that is NOT the shipped subset
data/_raw/

# The source workspaces live as SIBLINGS and are NEVER committed here — this repo
# is public (GitHub Pages) and must contain only our authored design surface:
#   ../dd-mods       (mod project: raw notes, .py tools)
#   ../_dd_extract   (datamine wiki, decompiled source + the 730MB asset export
#                     that sync-icons.mjs pulls the shipped icons FROM)
# If either is ever nested under this repo, ignore it:
# _*_extract/
# dd-mods/

# NOTE: data.js IS committed on purpose — GitHub Pages serves it directly.
# The data/*.json sources (incl. *.enrich.json + icon-sources.json) are committed
# too: they're the buildable source that regenerates data.js and assets/icons/.
